0..89 Comment "// `transport` computes on every filler that resolves, and stays stuck on a carried cell."
90..92 Comment "//"
93..165 Comment "// Nothing about a filler is primitive. A filler comes from completion\'s"
166..236 Comment "// derivation, from the filler generator or from a composite of cells."
237..239 Comment "//"
240..315 Comment "// `transport` over a generated filler and over a composite of `here` cells"
316..393 Comment "// reduces to its motive\'s base. The circle\'s `loop` stays stuck by name. The"
394..455 Comment "// row over completion\'s filler stands beside its derivation."
456..458 Comment "//"
459..526 Comment "// - see: `derived-rule.gandr` — the row over completion\'s filler"
527..594 Comment "// - see: `compose-chain.gandr` — unbiased composition of a chain"
596..634 Comment "// The circle, its point and its loop."
